Rules:
  [R1] Use exchanges for routing.
  [R2] Use queues for buffering.
  [R3] Use bindings for routing rules.
  [R4] Use acknowledgments for reliability.
  [R5] Use dead letter exchanges for failures.
  [R6] Use topic exchanges for flexibility.
  [R7] Use competing consumers for scaling.
  [R8] Monitor with RabbitMQ Management.

Pros:
  - Flexible routing
  - Reliable delivery
  - Good tooling

Cons:
  - Operational overhead
  - Clustering complexity
  - Memory usage

Alternatives:
  - Kafka (event streaming)
  - NATS (simpler)
  - AWS SQS (managed)

State: +

